@module_doc("""
Function introspection (experimental): read a function value as plain
records and lists.

The builtins are global, and their result shapes may still change.
[Function Introspection](features/function-introspection.md) is the full
description: every field, `code_hash`, the nodes of the tree, and the limits.
""")

# Package `core`, module `introspect` (docs/features/function-introspection.md).
#
# Native interface declarations: each `native fn` binds a name to the host
# native of the same name and gives the checker its parameter names, arity
# and types. Several declarations of one name are that native's call forms.
# See docs/usage/ffi.md (Native interfaces).

@doc("""
A record describing the function `f` (a lambda or a named `fn`): `name`,
`file`, `line`, `column`, `params`, `returns`, `captures` and `code_hash`.
`nil` for a builtin and for an overloaded name. See
[`fn_info`](features/function-introspection.md#fn_infof).
""",
  returns: """`{name, file, line, column, params, returns, captures, code_hash}`, or `nil`.""",
  see: ["fn_ast"])
pub native fn fn_info(f: function) -> record?

@doc("""
The function's syntax tree as nested records, each with a `tag`. `nil` when
there is no source to read (a builtin, an overloaded name, a class
constructor, a program loaded from IR). See
[`fn_ast`](features/function-introspection.md#fn_astf).
""",
  see: ["fn_info"])
pub native fn fn_ast(f: function) -> record?
